# Legacy URLs from earlier site platforms (GoDaddy/Wix, Bolt/React) that
# Google still has indexed and are now 404ing. 301s preserve link equity
# and stop repeat crawl errors during the platform transition.
# More specific rules must stay above the wildcards they'd otherwise
# shadow — Netlify uses first-match-wins.

# Old Wix blog post URL pattern (/blog/f/<slug>). Topical match for the
# one confirmed-indexed post; everything else under the old feed path
# falls back to the current blog index.
/blog/f/best-roofing-solutions-for-hot-dallas-summers  /blog/texas-heat-impacts-roof-lifespan  301
/blog/f/*  /blog  301

# Old top-level "/residential" page — no direct current equivalent, so
# it goes to the services hub, which covers residential roofing.
/residential  /services  301

# An earlier Astro build's canonical tags pointed city pages at
# /cities/<slug>, a route that never actually existed on this site
# (see README.md). Redirecting defensively in case that bad canonical
# got crawled and indexed before it was fixed.
/cities/*  /service-areas/:splat  301
